# =============================================================================
# Mirage native patch 0001 — fonts whitelist
# Target tag: 131.0.6778.85 (verify every anchor against this checkout)
# =============================================================================
#
# WHAT
#   Font enumeration is a measurement-side channel: a probe renders text with
#   `font-family: "<candidate>", monospace` and compares rendered metrics.
#   Closing it from JS is impossible without breaking rendering (see
#   inject/README.md, "Что сознательно НЕ перехватывается").
#
#   This patch gates Blink's system font resolution (FontCache::GetFontData)
#   with the whitelist from MIRAGE_FP_CONFIG ("fonts" field; same JSON schema
#   as window.__MIRAGE_FP__). A family outside the whitelist returns "not
#   found", so the CSS font matcher advances to the next family exactly as it
#   does for a font that is not installed — fallback metrics are identical to
#   an absent font. Families inside the whitelist resolve natively. Without
#   MIRAGE_FP_CONFIG the patch is completely inert.
#
# WHERE (candidates, in order of preference — block 3 resolves by signature):
#   1. third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc
#      — cross-platform entry point for family-name -> font resolution.
#        Search signals:
#          grep -n "FontCache::GetFontData" third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc
#          grep -n "FamilyShouldBeIgnored" third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/font_cache.cc
#            (if this helper exists in the tag, the gate belongs inside it —
#             it is the upstream hook for "family must resolve as absent")
#   2. third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/css_font_selector.cc
#      — CSS-side dispatcher (web fonts first, then FontCache).
#        Search signal: grep -n "GetFontData" third_party/blink/renderer/core/css/css_font_selector.cc
#   3. third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/win/font_cache_win.cc
#      — Windows-specific font creation; NOT the right gate (too low: generic
#        families are already resolved by then), but the source of truth for
#        the default standard/fixed fonts used in the always-allowed list.
#        Search signal: grep -n "Segoe UI" third_party/blink/renderer/platform/fonts/win/font_cache_win.cc
#
# KNOWN RESIDUALS (documented in patches/README.md, intentional):
#   - PlatformFallbackFontForCharacter (per-character fallback) is NOT gated:
#     blocking it would break CJK/emoji rendering on realistic pages. Profile
#     font lists are realistic full OS sets (fp-db/fonts.json), so the
#     whitelist already contains the fallback fonts of a real machine.
#   - local() in @font-face resolves through the same gate: a local() source
#     naming a non-whitelisted family fails — consistent with "not installed".
#   - document.fonts.check() consults the same resolution path and reports
#     blocked families as unavailable — consistent with "not installed".

